5. Constructive Significance and Criticality
A single 1D ranking (e.g., Primary > Secondary > Auxiliary) is mathematically and constructively insufficient because geometric importance and mechanical stability are orthogonal axes. Removing a fold can fail a structure in completely different ways:

Removing the nose-tip fold of a dart airplane alters length slightly (Geometrically Secondary) and changes nothing structurally.

Removing the final wing-root lock or fuselage crimp alters almost zero visible area (Geometrically Secondary), yet causes the wings to spring open and lose all aerodynamic dihedral (Mechanically Retention-Critical).

