6. Real Origami Examples
6.1 Classic Dart Paper Airplane (Nose, Keel, and Wing-Locking Assembly)
Shape-Creating Folds (ROLE_FORM):

Centerline longitudinal valley fold (establishes bilateral symmetry and fuselage spine).

Nose-narrowing diagonal folds (establish the pointed delta-wing planform).

Horizontal wing-root mountain folds (define the lifting wing surfaces vs. vertical keel).

Structural Folds (ROLE_STRUCT):

The combination of the centerline valley and two parallel wing-root mountain folds creates a Y- or V-shaped beam cross-section, providing longitudinal bending stiffness so the nose does not droop in flight.   
